## � Development Phases

### **Phase 1: Foundation & Basic UI** ⭐ *Start Here*
**Goal:** Get the app structure running with basic input capabilities

- [ ] Initialize React app and install core dependencies
- [ ] Set up project structure (components/, services/, views/)
- [ ] Create basic routing (Home, Designer, Order views)
- [ ] Build CabinetForm component with basic inputs
  - [ ] Cabinet type selector
  - [ ] Width, height, depth inputs
  - [ ] Material thickness input
- [ ] Implement basic state management (Redux/Zustand)
- [ ] Add form validation with React Hook Form
- [ ] Style with basic CSS (responsiveness comes later)

**Deliverable:** Working form that captures cabinet specifications

---

### **Phase 2: Calculation Engine**
**Goal:** Generate accurate part dimensions with joinery logic

- [ ] Create calculation service module
- [ ] Implement basic box geometry calculations
  - [ ] Top, bottom, sides dimensions
  - [ ] Back panel calculations
- [ ] Add joinery offset logic
  - [ ] Dado joint calculations
  - [ ] Rabbet joint calculations
  - [ ] Finger/box joint calculations
- [ ] Implement shelf calculations
  - [ ] Fixed shelf positioning
  - [ ] Adjustable shelf dados
- [ ] Add divider logic (vertical partitions)
- [ ] Integrate clipper-lib for geometry operations
- [ ] Create part list data structure

**Deliverable:** Accurate part dimensions based on inputs and joinery type

---

### **Phase 3: Visualization**
**Goal:** Show users what they're designing

- [ ] Build PartPreview component (simple 2D schematic)
- [ ] Create interactive cabinet diagram
  - [ ] Show assembled view
  - [ ] Label major components
- [ ] Implement grain direction indicators
- [ ] Add basic SVG/Canvas rendering
- [ ] Create color-coding system for part types
- [ ] Show real-time updates as form changes

**Deliverable:** Visual representation of cabinet design

---

### **Phase 4: Nesting & Layout**
**Goal:** Optimize part arrangement on sheet materials

- [ ] Integrate SVGNest or rectpack2D
- [ ] Create SheetLayout component
- [ ] Implement material sheet size configuration
- [ ] Build nesting algorithm integration
- [ ] Add grain direction respect in nesting
- [ ] Calculate material waste/efficiency
- [ ] Show multiple sheet layouts if needed
- [ ] Add manual adjustment capability (drag parts)

**Deliverable:** Optimized sheet layout with minimal waste

---

### **Phase 5: Export Functionality**
**Goal:** Generate production-ready files

- [ ] Integrate dxf-writer library
- [ ] Build DXF export service
  - [ ] Generate layers (cut, pocket, drill)
  - [ ] Add part labels to DXF
  - [ ] Include dimension annotations
- [ ] Create CSV cut list export (PapaParse)
  - [ ] Part name, dimensions, quantity
  - [ ] Material type, grain direction
- [ ] Implement PDF generation (jsPDF)
  - [ ] Cut list printout
  - [ ] Assembly diagram
- [ ] Add ZIP bundling (JSZip)
  - [ ] Package all exports together
  - [ ] Include metadata file
- [ ] Build download UI components

**Deliverable:** Complete export system with DXF, CSV, PDF, and ZIP

